    "restoration_notes": "Large multipurpose fruit tree providing edible fruit, timber, and natural insecticidal compounds. Well suited for diversified cacao agroforestry systems. Long-lived canopy species that contributes structural diversity to restoration landscapes. Grafted planting material is strongly recommended to reduce the long juvenile period and avoid non-productive male trees. Requires deep, fertile, well-drained soils and performs poorly in compacted or waterlogged sites. Within FYNOS AI, it is recommended as a complementary productive canopy species rather than a primary native Amazon restoration tree."
